\[2x = 2\sqrt{6}\]
\[x = \sqrt{6}\]

Now, the lengths of the legs are \(\sqrt{6}\) and \(\sqrt{3}\).

The sum of the lengths of the two legs is:
\[\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{3}\]

Therefore, the sum of the lengths of the two legs is \(\boxed{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{3}}
