\[
9 \times 10^8
\]

Calculating this:

\[
9 \times 10^8 = 9 \times 100000000 = 9000000000
\]

Thus, the number of possible 9-digit zip codes where the first digit cannot be zero is \(\boxed{9000000000}\).
