Problem:
Let $u,$ $v,$ $w$ be the roots of $z^3 = 1.$  Find $uv + uw + vw.$

Solution:
answer:  The roots of the equation $z^3 = 1$ are the cube roots of unity, which are $1,$ $e^{2\pi i / 3},$ and $e^{-2\pi i / 3}.$

We need to find $uv + uw + vw.$

Let $u = 1,$ $v = e^{2\pi i / 3},$ and $w = e^{-2\pi i / 3}.$

Then,
\begin{align*}
uv + uw + vw &= 1 \cdot e^{2\pi i / 3} + 1 \cdot e^{-2\pi i / 3} + e^{2\pi i / 3} \cdot e^{-2\pi i / 3} \\
&= e^{2\pi i / 3} + e^{-2\pi i / 3} + 1 \\
&= 1 + 1 + 1 \\
&= \boxed{3}.
\end{align*}
