answer:  We know that $\mathbf{D} \mathbf{R}$ is a rotation matrix followed by a dilation matrix. The rotation matrix $\mathbf{R}$ has the form $\begin{pmatrix} \cos \theta & -\sin \theta \\ \sin \theta & \cos \theta \end{pmatrix}$ and the dilation matrix $\mathbf{D}$ has the form $\begin{pmatrix} k & 0 \\ 0 & k \end{pmatrix}$. Therefore, $\mathbf{D} \mathbf{R}$ has the form $\begin{pmatrix} k \cos \theta & -k \sin \theta \\ k \sin \theta & k \cos \theta \end{pmatrix}$.

