\[ \sin 2t = 2 \sin t \cos t \]

Substituting \( x = \sin t \) into the equation for \( y \):
\[ y = 2 \sin t \cos t \]

We know that:
\[ \sin t \cos t = \frac{1}{2} x^2 \]

Thus:
\[ y = 2 \left( \frac{1}{2} x^2 \right) = x^2 \]

