Problem:
Compute $\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} -11 \\ 10 \end{pmatrix}$.

Solution:
answer:  To add the vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} -11 \\ 10 \end{pmatrix}\), we add the corresponding components of the vectors.

\[
\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} -11 \\ 10 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 + (-11) \\ -4 + 10 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
\]

Therefore, the result is \(\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}}\).
