2. The period of \(\cos(x)\) is also \(2\pi\).

When we consider \(\cos(\sin(x))\), the inner function \(\sin(x)\) completes one full cycle every \(2\pi\). Therefore, the outer function \(\cos(x)\) will also complete one full cycle every \(2\pi\).

Thus, the least period of \(\cos(\sin(x))\) is \(2\pi\).

Final Answer: The final answer is \(2\pi\).
