Problem:
The points $O,$ $A,$ and $B$ satisfy $\overrightarrow{OA} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\overrightarrow{OB} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}.$  Find the area of triangle $OAB.$

Solution:
answer:  The area of triangle $OAB$ is given by the magnitude of the cross product of $\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\overrightarrow{OB}$. We have

$$\overrightarrow{OA} \times \overrightarrow{OB} = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\ -3 & -2 & 1 \end{vmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ -7 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix}.$$

The magnitude of this vector is

$$\sqrt{(-5)^2 + (-7)^2 + (-4)^2} = \sqrt{25 + 49 + 16} = \sqrt{90}.$$

Therefore, the area of triangle $OAB$ is $\boxed{\sqrt{90}}$.
