Problem:
Compute $\tan \left( \arccos \frac{1}{3} \right).$

Solution:
answer:  We know that $\cos \left( \arccos \frac{1}{3} \right) = \frac{1}{3}$. Therefore, $\sin \left( \arccos \frac{1}{3} \right) = \sqrt{1 - \left( \frac{1}{3} \right)^2} = \sqrt{1 - \frac{1}{9}} = \sqrt{\frac{8}{9}} = \frac{\sqrt{8}}{3}$. Thus, $\tan \left( \arccos \frac{1}{3} \right) = \frac{\sin \left( \arccos \frac{1}{3} \right)}{\cos \left( \arccos \frac{1}{3} \right)} = \frac{\frac{\sqrt{8}}{3}}{\frac{1}{3}} = \frac{\sqrt{8}}{3}$.
