Problem:
The point $P$ on the sphere of radius 3 and centered at the origin has spherical coordinate $\left( 3, \frac{3 \pi}{8}, \frac{\pi}{5} \right).$  Find the spherical coordinates of the point diametrically opposite $P.$  Enter your answer in the form $(\rho,\theta,\phi),$ where $\rho > 0,$ $0 \le \theta < 2 \pi,$ and $0 \le \phi \le \pi.$

Solution:
answer:  The point diametrically opposite $P$ on the sphere will have the same radius $\rho$ and the same azimuthal angle $\theta$, but its polar angle $\phi$ will be $\pi - \phi$. Therefore, the spherical coordinates of the point diametrically opposite $P$ are:

$$\left( 3, \frac{3 \pi}{8}, \pi - \frac{\pi}{5} \right) = \left( 3, \frac{3 \pi}{8}, \frac{4\pi}{5} \right)$$

