Problem:
Find the matrix that corresponds to projecting onto the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}.$

Solution:
answer:  The projection matrix onto a vector $\mathbf{v}$ is given by $\frac{\mathbf{v} \mathbf{v}^T}{\mathbf{v}^T \mathbf{v}}.$ Here, $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix},$ so the projection matrix is

$$\frac{\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}^T}{\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}^T \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}} = \frac{\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 7 \\ 7 & 49 \end{pmatrix}}{\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 7 \\ 7 & 49 \end{pmatrix}} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}.$$

Therefore, the matrix that corresponds to projecting onto the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}$ is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}}.$ Answer: answer is $\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}$. I is correct
