Problem:
Simplify $$2\cos^2(\log(2009)i)+i\sin(\log(4036081)i).$$Note: The logarithms are with respect to base $e.$

Solution:
answer:  First, we simplify the expressions inside the logarithms:

$$\log(2009) = \log(43^2) = 2\log(43)$$
$$\log(4036081) = \log(43^4) = 4\log(43)$$

Next, we substitute these values back into the expression:

$$2\cos^2(2\log(43)i) + i\sin(4\log(43)i)$$

Now, we use the properties of the cosine and sine functions:

$$\cos^2(2\log(43)i) = 1$$
$$\sin(4\log(43)i) = 0$$

So, the expression simplifies to:

$$2(1) + i(0) = 2 + 0 = \boxed{2}$$
